Abstract = {When Sydney's 760ha Homebush Bay industrial site was rezoned for urban
   renewal and staging the Olympic Games in 2000, massive investment was
   made to remediate past damage and develop a future public park
   containing active recreation and natural areas. Since that date,
   endangered forest and wetland communities, along with threatened fauna
   species, have received priority treatments to improve the ecological
   function of the Park's natural areas. Evaluation of progress 12years on
   reveals substantial achievements and multiple lessons.},
